  if (this.files && this.files[0]) {
    readCSVFile(this.files[0]);
  }
});
```

In this example, we create a function called `readCSVFile` that takes a file as its argument. We use the `FileReader` API to read the contents of the file as text. Once the file has been loaded, we split the text into lines and then further split each line into fields based on commas. Finally, we log each field to the console.

To use this function, you would need to have an HTML element (like an `<input type="file">`) where users can select their CSV files. The above script listens for changes to this input element and calls `readCSVFile` whenever a new file is selected.

