<fieldset><legend>Answer:</legend>
To implement a rate limiter in your PHP application using Redis, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the Predis library for interacting with Redis in PHP:
   ```
   composer require predis/predis
   ```

2. Create a new class called RateLimiter with the following code:

```php
use Predis\Client;

class RateLimiter
{
    private $client;
    private $limit;
    private $interval;

    public function __construct(Client $client, int $limit, int $interval)
    {
        $this->client = $client;
        $this->limit = $limit;
        $this->interval = $interval;
    }

    public function allowRequest(string $key): bool
    {
        $currentTimestamp = time();
        $windowStart = $currentTimestamp - $this->interval;

        // Get the current count of requests within the interval
        $count = $this->client->zCount($key, $windowStart, $currentTimestamp);

        if ($count >= $this->limit) {
            return false;
        }

        // Add the current request timestamp to the sorted set
        $this->client->zAdd($key, ['score' => $currentTimestamp, 'member' => $currentTimestamp]);

        return true;
    }
}
```

3. Use the RateLimiter class in your application:

```php
$client = new Client();

$rateLimiter = new RateLimiter($client, 5, 60); // Allow 5 requests per minute

$key = 'my_rate_limited_resource';

if ($rateLimiter->allowRequest($key)) {
    // Process the request
} else {
    // Return an error response indicating the user has exceeded the rate limit
}
```

This implementation uses Redis' sorted sets to store timestamps of recent requests. By checking the size of the sorted set within a specific time window, you can determine whether a user has exceeded the allowed number of requests. Adjust the `$limit` and `$interval` values according to your desired rate-limiting policy.</fieldset>fieldset<legend>Question:</legend>
